Technical Challenges and Market Constraints

GNSS performance can be affected by buildings, tunnels, interference, multipath signals and environmental conditions. Receivers must manage weak signals and maintain reliable positioning under the conditions expected in their intended applications.

Higher-precision products can involve increased hardware, antenna and service costs. Device manufacturers must also consider compatibility with satellite constellations, correction services and downstream software platforms.

